From: Marc Herrero <marcht@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: use 32-bit container for S24_LE PCM

SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE carries 24 valid bits in a 32-bit container, but
audioreach_shmem_set_media_format() and audioreach_pcm_set_media_format()
(PARAM_ID_MEDIA_FORMAT and PARAM_ID_PCM_OUTPUT_FORMAT_CFG) set
bits_per_sample = bit_width = 24, i.e. tell the DSP the samples are
packed 3-byte words.

On QCS6490 (Radxa Dragon Q6A, sc8280xp machine driver) playing S24_LE on
a q6apm-dai front end with a topology that allows it makes the ADSP
audio_process crash:

  PDM: service 'audio_process' crash: 'EX:audio_process:0x2:...'
  q6apm-lpass-dais ...: Failed to start APM port 113
  remoteproc remoteproc0: crash detected in adsp: type fatal error

Set bits_per_sample to the container size (32) for 24-bit data, keeping
bit_width = 24, alignment = PCM_LSB_ALIGNED and q_factor = 23. With this
change S24_LE playback works on the headphone path (codec DMA RX ->
lpass rx macro -> WCD9385), with the back end at S16_LE, S24_LE or
S32_LE and 48/96/192 kHz.

Note that the DSP then reads the whole 32-bit word as Q23, so S24_LE data
must be sign-extended into the top byte. alsa-lib's conversions do this;
an application that leaves the top byte at zero (seen with shairport-sync)
plays heavily distorted.

Signed-off-by: Marc Herrero <marcht@proton.me>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c	2026-11-11 08:34:08.238639713 +0000
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c	2026-11-11 08:34:08.246088306 +0000
@@ -1112,7 +1112,7 @@
 	media_cfg->interleaved = module->interleave_type;
 	media_cfg->num_channels = mcfg->num_channels;
 	media_cfg->q_factor = mcfg->bit_width - 1;
-	media_cfg->bits_per_sample = mcfg->bit_width;
+	media_cfg->bits_per_sample = mcfg->bit_width == 24 ? 32 : mcfg->bit_width;
 	memcpy(media_cfg->channel_mapping, mcfg->channel_map, mcfg->num_channels);
 
 	return q6apm_send_cmd_sync(graph->apm, pkt, 0);
@@ -1198,7 +1198,7 @@
 		cfg->sample_rate = mcfg->sample_rate;
 		cfg->bit_width = mcfg->bit_width;
 		cfg->alignment = PCM_LSB_ALIGNED;
-		cfg->bits_per_sample = mcfg->bit_width;
+		cfg->bits_per_sample = mcfg->bit_width == 24 ? 32 : mcfg->bit_width;
 		cfg->q_factor = mcfg->bit_width - 1;
 		cfg->endianness = PCM_LITTLE_ENDIAN;
 		cfg->num_channels = mcfg->num_channels;
